#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# asymptotic_greater_equal

#% text
# `asymptotic_greater_equal(f, g, x -> a)` gives true when g = O(f) as x approaches a: |g/f| stays bounded near a.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# It is `asymptotic_less_equal(g, f, x -> a)`, with the same options `direction:` and `assumptions:`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
asymptotic_greater_equal(x^2, x, x -> inf)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
asymptotic_greater_equal(x, x^2, x -> inf)
#% output
#= false

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `asymptotic_less_equal`, `asymptotic_greater`, `asymptotic_equal`
